      "text": "Let's denote Mateen's backyard's length as \\( L \\) meters and its width as \\( W \\) meters. We are given the following conditions:\n\n1. **Perimeter Approach:**\n\n   Mateen needs to traverse the perimeter 10 times to walk a kilometer:\n   \\[\n   10 \\times (2L + 2W) = 1000 \\, \\text{meters}\n   \\]\n   \n   Simplifying the equation:\n   \\[\n   10 \\times 2(L + W) = 1000 \\implies 2(L + W) = 100 \\implies L + W = 50\n   \\]\n\n2. **Length Approach:**\n\n   Mateen must walk the length 25 times to cover the kilometer:\n   \\[\n   25L = 1000 \\, \\text{meters}\n   \\]\n   \n   Solving for \\( L \\):\n   \\[\n   L = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\, \\text{meters}\n   \\]\n\nWith both approaches, we have determined Mateen’s backyard has:\n\\[ L = 40 \\, \\text{meters} \\]\n\\[ W = 50 \\, \\text{meters} \\]\n\n3. **Area Calculation:**\n\n   To find the area \\( A \\) of the rectangular backyard:\n   \\[\n   A = L \\times W = 40 \\times 50 = 2000 \\, \\text{square meters}\n   \\]\n\nConclusion: The area of Mateen's backyard is \\boxed{2000} square meters.",
