      "text": "1. The perimeter of the backyard is an even number, so the length $l$ of the backyard must be an even number. 2. In order to walk the length 25 times, Mateen must first walk the perimeter $k$ times, so $kl = \\text{perimeter}$. 3. Walking the perimeter 10 times is the distance Mateen has walked without walking the length of his backyard, so $k = 10$. 4. As $kl = \\text{perimeter}$ and $k = 10$, we can find the perimeter $p$ as follows: $p = 25l = 25(10) = \\boxed{250}$. 5. We are asked to find the area of his backyard. 6. As $p$ and $l$ are known, we can calculate the area as follows: $p = 2l + 2w$, so $w = \\frac{p - p}{2} = \\frac{250}{2} = \\boxed{125}$.",
